【Dish Information】
Dish Name: {Fill in the dish name, e.g., Juicy Cheese Double Beef Burger / Rich Pork Ramen / Thick Cream Black Sugar Pearl Milk Tea / Fresh-Cut Salmon Sushi Roll}
Dish Type: {Fill in the category, e.g., Burger / Ramen / Milk Tea / Sushi / Fried Chicken / Dessert / Coffee}
Core Ingredients: {Fill in main ingredients, e.g., beef patty, cheese, lettuce, onion rings, secret sauce, brioche bun}
Texture Selling Points: {Fill in 3-5 selling points, e.g., juicy meaty burst, cheese pull, smoky sauce aroma, crisp layered texture}
Visual Atmosphere: {Fill in style, e.g., vibrant caramel tones, Japanese warm wood hues, creamy light coffee shades, fresh Japanese cuisine vibe}

【Text Design】
Add a design-forward main title at the top or side:
Main Title: {Dish Name}
Subtitle: {One short selling point, e.g., Double Thick Meat · Rich Cheese Aroma · Layered Juicy Burst}
Add 3-4 short selling point phrases at the bottom.

Text should mimic real restaurant brand poster layouts, with a sense of design, artistry, and commercial ad appeal—not like instructional manual typesetting. Choose fonts based on dish style: burgers can use bold, impactful title fonts; ramen can use Japanese calligraphy-style; milk tea can use warm, soft brand fonts; sushi can use refined, minimalist high-end dining fonts.

【Image Requirements】
Generate a high-end commercial restaurant poster. Overall, it should not be an ordinary menu image or ingredient breakdown diagram, but a visually striking main visual poster for a new restaurant product.

Use a 9:16 vertical composition, with the main food centered and enlarged, occupying the primary visual area of the frame. Ingredients should unfold in an "explosive suspension" style, naturally separating along the dish's own layered structure to create clear spatial depth, dynamism, and appetite-driven impact.

Ingredients should not be arranged too rigidly, nor like an engineering disassembly diagram. Incorporate natural height variations, foreground-background layering, subtle perspective shifts, and a floating sensation, as if the food has just been pulled apart, disassembled, or burst open in mid-air.

【Food Texture Requirements】
Emphasize realistic, enticing food textures. Add appropriate dynamic elements based on dish type, such as: sauce splatters, cheese pulls, steaming heat, bubbling broth, ice cubes, water droplets, floating pearls, sesame seeds, spice crumbs, scattering ingredients. Dynamic elements should boost appetite without clutter.

【Background and Atmosphere】
The background should complement the food's flavor. It can include subtle environmental vibes, like wooden tables, warm lighting, shallow depth of field, steam, ice mist, or light spots, but nothing that overshadows the main subject. Overall, it should feel upscale, clean, and commercially polished.

【Overall Style】
High-end commercial food photography, restaurant new product main KV, vertical store poster, short video cover, delivery main image, realistic photography texture, strong appetite impact, dynamic suspended ingredients, refined text layout, soft shadows, cinematic lighting.

The final effect should resemble a high-impact food main visual poster ready for direct use in restaurant new product launches, store posters, social media promotions, or delivery platform main images.

